WEBVTT

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.100
Yoshinoya

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.670
Yoshinoya
It's morning! Wake up already!

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.110
It's morning! Wake up already!

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.310
Wake up! You're going to be late!

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.280
It's almost 10 o'clock!

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.750
Wake up already!

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.820
Please enter the revival spell.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.060
That is the wrong spell.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.790
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.640
Question, question, question,
question, question mark

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.010
Lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing about

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.940
What should we do?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.120
For now, let's just yell "Wasshoi!"

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.650
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.050
Wa! Shoi!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.720
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.730
Even an absurd response

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.630
Is sensible for someone from Jupiter

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.730
Launch a rocket at random

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.570
And approach the place where it lands

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:22.230
After a pleasant nap

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.640
Sure enough, sure enough,
my eyes tear when I yawn

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:27.810
Good morning

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.980
Let's play!

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.680
Let's have a serious bread-eating race

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.820
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.350
Who, who, who, who, who is it?

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.690
Hungry, hungry, hungry,
hungry, hungry person

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:43.090
Girls live off snacks

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.860
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:45.660
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.000
Lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing about

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.900
Let's look up at the sun

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.170
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.710
In a dream, in a dream with everyone
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.280
I had the same conversation

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.180
Question mark and washoi 365

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.980
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.520
August 5, Restless Summer

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.460
Jeez!

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:25.060
Why do teachers have to go to
school during the summer?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.960
Don't you know?

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.160
We have no classes,
but we have a lot of work to do.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:35.240
This is the work you have to do.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.550
This much?!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.980
You have this much because you've
been procrastinating.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.250
I'm going to make you do it.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.650
T-Tomorrow...

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.090
Please do it!

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.520
I can't today...

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.460
Do it!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.520
Escape

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.570
I don't want to run away, but...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.760
Art Preparation Room

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.940
Today, Yoshinoya had something she had to do.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.610
She had to make a summer greeting card.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:16.280
She had to make the special summer
greeting card she makes every year.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.090
I'm going to do my best!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.050
Oh?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.460
That's why...

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.360
It looks like they're having fun today!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.520
Flash!

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.210
Good morning!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.210
M-Ms. Yoshinoya!

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.570
Why are you dressed as a race queen?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:51.110
I am always watching you fight in
the race circuit known as art!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.790
I'm not sure I understand.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.050
Also, I don't want to get sunburned.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.750
Are you all going to class now?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.390
Yes, we're going to do our summer
homework in class.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:07.300
I see. Well, keep up the good work.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.670
Thank you very much.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:09.740
See you later.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.640
Fight!

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.340
Ms. Yoshinoya!

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:14.430
Oh no!

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.680
No!

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.020
The principal is too strict.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:31.550
It's not as if I don't do any work.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.760
She can put off her work until later.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.960
Right now, she has summer
greeting cards to make.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.300
That seems about right.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.940
Next is...

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.400
Tadaa!

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.740
She leaves costumes at school so that
she can wear them at any time.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.270
I've got more!

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.250
I knew you'd come here.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.550
Now get back to work!

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.690
All right, time to get started!

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.050
Needless to say, she takes all
of her pictures herself.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.840
I guess I can move my photo shoot.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.560
Health Room

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.640
It's only natural that the principal
would get mad.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.670
What? What do you mean?

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:51.840
Can't you tell?

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.900
Not at all.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.900
I know what kind of person you are.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.550
But I won't give up!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.080
Growl...

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.190
Come to think of it,
we still haven't had lunch.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.650
Wonton ramen!

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.390
Thank you for ordering from Manpukuken!

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.690
We've been waiting for you!

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.590
Three cold Chinese noodles!

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.600
Thank you for your hard work in this heat.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.970
I have some barley tea. Would you like some?

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.600
Oh, thank you.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:26.700
It looks delicious! Let's dig in!

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.210
Ms. Yoshinoya...

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.540
Once you're done eating lunch,
you're going back to work.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.620
I don't feel like it.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.280
That was blunt.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.550
That's because there aren't any students.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.750
I wonder how everyone's doing?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.430
It looks like it's going to continue to be hot.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.130
I want second semester to come quickly.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:56.170
Yeah, the school is too quiet without students.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:59.440
Things have been pretty busy though.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:02.080
I want to be with everyone!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.510
I want to escape the principal's
man-mark defense.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.480
It's the warning bell.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.210
Thank you for the food!

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.550
Thank you very much!

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:21.920
Quit Smoking

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.160
I'm going to quit next time!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.360
Let's meet again at school.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.940
I've completed 2B's cards!

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:37.400
Yoshinoya sends summer greeting
cards to all of her students.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.620
Not only the ones at school,
but also the ones who graduated.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.880
Excuse me, I'd like to use your printer.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.950
Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.050
Oh, Natsume.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.930
What are you doing?

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.900
No, don't look at it yet!

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.300
Wait until I send it to you!

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.830
U-Umm, I can wait until you're
done using your printer.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.970
Are you leaving?

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:07.040
Then, can I ask you a favor?

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:07.740
Huh?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.470
I want people to see these
as soon as possible.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.470
Why am I doing this?

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.810
I'd hate it if Sae saw me!

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:21.320
No one's coming out...

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:27.930
I got something.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:28.560
Summer Greetings

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.890
Summer Greetings
Wow!

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.400
Ms. Yoshinoya is incredible.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.970
I worked very hard!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.070
She finally completed her
summer greeting cards.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.100
Tomorrow, she has to begin her
late summer greeting cards.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.150
Get to work already.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:48.120
Huh?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.820
My head hurts. I have a fever.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.420
It's probably a developmental fever.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.650
Ms. Kuwahara, I thought
that you were my ally.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.000
I'm sticking around with you.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.260
But you're not helping me.
You're just watching.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:16.310
Did you become one of the principal's spies?

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.300
Ms. Yoshinoya...

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.140
Let's play with these after you finish.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.910
O-Okay.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:37.700
Wow! They're beautiful!

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.000
It's been a long time since
I played with fireworks!

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.000
Yeah...

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.730
Hey, look at this!

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.500
A heart!

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.670
She really is a handful.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:58.150
But she cherishes her students and has
a never-ending passion for art.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:10.790
I hope everyone receives their summer
greeting cards by tomorrow.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.590
I hope they like them!

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.860
I'm going to work hard on my
late summer greeting cards!

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.740
Summer Greetings

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.800
August 5
The End
To Be Continued

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:26.850
One
One.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:27.810
One.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.620
Good morning.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:51.710
Okay.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.300
Yunocchi!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.840
Coming!

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.850
Repent!
December 3, The Urashinjuku Wolf Part 2
Repent!

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.540
Asagi Housing Complex

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.950
I hope it comes quickly.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.380
I feel cold standing still.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.460
Is that from Miya-chan?

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.690
That's right!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.420
A letter? You live in the same apartment.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.850
There are things you can only say by letter.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.120
I'll write you my response later.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.090
Okay.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:26.270
I've been constantly checking to see
if I have it since this morning.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:28.170
The Wolf of Urashinjuku?

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:32.010
An independent screening, huh?

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.040
I wonder what it's like?

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.720
Let's make a dash for it when
we get to our stop.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.120
What seats do you want?

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:41.380
Someplace that has four seats
next to each other.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:44.580
I hope we can find good seats.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.030
Yeah!

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:49.150
This is the movie that Kishi made.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.960
Is the bus coming?

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.310
Don't cry.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:00.930
We'll meet again.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.440
I know we will.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:11.410
Yeah, no matter what form I'm
reborn in, I will surely...

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:17.290
No!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:23.950
The End

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.240
That was great, wasn't it, honey?

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.110
It sure was, darling.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.650
It's so warm!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.620
Kotatsu sure are great.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.590
Thank you for waiting. I've got hot cocoa.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:47.750
Thank you.

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.910
It's so warm!

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:56.820
Didn't any of you have anywhere
you wanted to stop by?

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:59.730
We ended up coming straight back, didn't we?

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:03.670
I was thinking about things on our bus back.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.440
Before I knew it, we had arrived at our stop.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.530
What were you thinking about?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.150
All sorts of things.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:14.310
I was feeling kind of depressed.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.110
Do you dislike sad stories?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.110
No, but isn't it sad?

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:25.030
Seeing those two try to stay together
even though they know they can't

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:29.930
is depressing and not very uplifting.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:33.830
It would be a little different
if it had a happy ending.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.210
Sae, that's so cool!

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.870
A true professional writer.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:40.810
Huh?

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:43.970
Well, it's not that big of a deal.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.520
I was just distracted by the beautiful scenery.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:53.920
Right? The overall use of color
was really beautiful.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:58.590
Kishi is really amazing to be able
to create a film like that.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:01.130
Yuno, did you talk to Kishi?

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.690
Yes, just a little though.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:06.930
Kishi!

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.000
It's you...

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:14.780
Umm, I don't think you remember me,
but I'm a student at Yamabuki High School.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:17.080
Ms. Yoshinoya's class, right?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.680
That's right!

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:23.020
Ms. Yoshinoya gave me some tickets,
so I came to watch.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.140
Thank you!

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:31.050
Umm, it was very beautiful and lovely!

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:34.930
Thank you.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.260
Mai, keep up the good work!

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.000
There sure were a lot of viewers.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.530
Some of them were even standing.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:46.940
I didn't notice that.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:50.900
It sure is impressive to have one of your
creations seen by lots of people.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:54.940
I wonder if Kishi is eventually going
to release it across the country?

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.680
Kishi would do it.

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:58.120
You're right.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.720
I want to see Kishi's movie again.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.620
It sure was interesting.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.490
It made me realize that it's possible
to express yourself using film.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.630
If you were a director, I wonder what
kind of movie you would make?

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:15.190
I'd like to do a suspense-musical.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.400
Huh?

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.070
The main character would sing as
he chases down the culprit.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:22.800
And he'd dance when he's in danger.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.140
Wouldn't that be a comedy?

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.920
Kishi sure is impressive.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:36.190
She followed her dreams. What will I do?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:41.320
I can't decide what I want to do.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.590
But...

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.440
Wow!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.740
What?!

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.300
Whoa!

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:02.110
Deep fried pies filled with
shrimp and avocado...

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.920
Spring rolls and tofu fried in sesame oil...

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.390
Carrot potage...

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.850
Japanese-style lasagna filled
with meat and potatoes...

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.180
And tuna with cheese!

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.060
What's all this, Hiro?

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.030
I felt like doing something.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.000
It seems like a waste to eat it.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.230
It's arranged so beautifully.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.570
I can't hold back any longer!

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.940
I'm digging in!

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:29.780
It's delicious!

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:30.880
Miyako...

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.110
Yuno, Sae, have some.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.170
Well, thank you for the food.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.080
What should I eat first?

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.280
Umm, thank you for the food.

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.090
Delicious! It's so mellow!

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.220
Crunchy and soft!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:47.790
Healthy!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:50.930
Wow, strong!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.030
Japanese-style!

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:58.170
The tuna and the cheese are
a superb combination!

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.710
Yeah! It's delicious!

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:01.880
Thank goodness!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.640
I still haven't eaten any of it.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:05.480
This is bliss!

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:06.410
Thank you.

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:07.950
What were all of you doing?

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.680
I was writing a novel.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:10.720
A new one?

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:14.320
Yeah, I've had something in
my head for a while.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.290
I tried putting it to paper
and things got rolling.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.220
Oh?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:17.490
Physics 1

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.830
Physics 1
I did this!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.320
Are you doing physics?

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:22.790
Oh my!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.490
What is it?

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.070
You scribbled on your textbook.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.940
Still, it's impressive.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.910
We're in the middle of a meal, you know.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:34.340
You're right.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:35.740
What were you doing, Yuno?

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:44.080
I drew images that came to mind.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.820
That sounds great.

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:48.410
Yeah, it's cool!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.720
New

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.760
This commercial is still running?

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.360
When is it going on sale?

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.630
As always, it says it's coming soon.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:02.170
It's terrible of them to run the
commercial but not put it on sale.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:05.210
It's probably best if we don't
expect it to go on sale.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.370
But...

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.110
It's shining!

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:07.710
It looks delicious!
It's shining!

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.570
It looks delicious!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.500
Good work!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.680
No matter how many times I look at this,
I'm still impressed.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.650
Let me see it once more.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.880
Go right ahead.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:22.390
Wow!

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.990
The fish becomes a bowl of rice.

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:27.560
Then a steak...

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.930
Then a potato...

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.870
Then a fish again. How odd!

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:34.460
Perhaps I should use my math
textbook for my next work.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.270
Maybe I'll use my
Japanese-English dictionary.

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:39.270
That will be a big work.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.540
Don't let the teachers see you.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.310
Naoi

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.580
Naoi
Sorry, excuse me.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.990
We should get going.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.080
Yeah!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.310
Thank you for the food!

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.280
I didn't take a look at it today.

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.590
Thank you for taking the time to remind me.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.620
Yes, I'll read it right away.

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:06.630
Thank you very much.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.500
Have you finally received a love letter?!

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:14.910
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:16.580
Who is it from?

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:17.740
It's not what you think it is!

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.850
That call was from my editor.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:25.320
The editorial department received a fan
letter for me, so they sent it over.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.480
Huh? A fan letter?

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:29.350
Yeah...

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:32.990
Ready?

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:35.000
Hiro!

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.460
You don't need to call her!

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.300
Honestly...

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:48.040
Is it really a love letter?

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.180
It isn't.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.810
What did he write?

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:58.190
He said that the novel I wrote in
last month's issue was good.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:59.320
Wow!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.820
Last month's issue?

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.220
Where? Let us see.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.220
Don't! It's not there.
Where? Let us see.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.620
Don't! It's not there.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:07.190
Congratulations.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:09.320
Is that appropriate?

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.900
I guess so.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.390
This is the first time you've received
a fan letter, isn't it?

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:17.500
I'm happy too!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.000
Yeah...

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:27.650
Tsk! She should let us read it.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.650
Sae's a real pro, isn't she?

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:32.890
She even has fans.

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:34.550
That's amazing!

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:38.490
It's kind of nerve-wracking to show
your works to others, isn't it?

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.880
And it's exciting!

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.860
I think it's just nerve-wracking for me.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.100
If someone likes your work...

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:53.200
It's a wonderful feeling, isn't it?

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.710
Are you feeling cold?

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.780
Do you want me you make some tea?

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:02.480
That's all right.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.020
I've got a big project I have to start on.

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:07.290
I see. Got it.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:08.520
What are you going to do, Yunocchi?

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.120
I'm going to prepare for tomorrow.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.460
We're painting with watercolors.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:12.580
Roger that.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.060
Well, goodnight.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:16.650
Goodnight.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:27.570
Everyone's amazing.

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:29.800
They're all so much better than I am.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.910
Someday, I'll be as good as they are.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:35.680
Dear Miya-chan...

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:39.590
Umm, you don't need to
worry about tomorrow.

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.680
Cover for me the next time I forget something.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:47.550
I've been fidgety ever since
I saw Kishi's movie.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:54.030
I really want to draw, but I don't know what.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:58.670
I want to draw.

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:01.800
I'm going to try my best!

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:05.540
Yuno...

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:09.680
December 3
The End
To Be Continued

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:25.430
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:31.170
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:38.210
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.010
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:50.080
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:55.660
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:57.260
Run all night

00:22:57.260 --> 00:23:00.330
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:03.670
Your singing voice

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:06.740
Touches my heart

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:10.010
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:10.010 --> 00:23:13.150
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:16.350
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:19.790
Leads me through space

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:22.660
A song about shooting stars

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:26.190
I can't hear them

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:30.130
I can't reach them

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:34.690
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:41.260
Preview

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:44.430
Preview
Say, how far back do your memories go?

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:47.900
Preview
Chika's go back to when she was born.
I was really shocked.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:50.330
Preview
Mine go back to about preschool.

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:51.870
Preview
Mine go back to when I was born!

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:53.240
Preview
What?!

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:56.840
Preview
Is it that strange? I remembered it
when I went scuba diving.

00:23:56.840 --> 00:24:01.580
Preview
When I surfaced, I thought,
"So, this is it. Waah!"

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:02.080
Preview

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:05.720
Preview
The next episode is
"June 8, Round Carrots"

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:07.250
Preview
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments.

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:09.120
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:09.980
Preview
